{"allowed_english": [], "context": {"approved_glossary_entries": [], "generation_contexts": [{"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale:inventory:etale:024X:example/0001", "hash": "sha256:f2ebc06282b961bb53366bfa4592036b131aea1e74dadef784c85fed0f427808", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 30109, "byte_start": 29101, "file": "etale.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:1c3138941131da6ea8968f4159e253def81d488ad4fade6df3f2885c5e6ef9d6", "line_end": 777, "line_start": 759}, "owner_tag": "024X", "parent_tag": "024W", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "024W", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "LOCKED_0001": "\\label{example-etale-field-extensions}", "MATH_0001": "$k$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to \\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$0$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$k$", "MATH_0008": "$A$", "MATH_0009": "$k$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0011": "$k$", "MATH_0012": "$X \\to \\Spec(k)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{example}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{example}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:07fe2da25a64ba25b10bd1020d2afac825f39461536d6185198d472db478aeca", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:70d45266879cf349c2447595613d66dffc494e3dc81f06ffb2d8d170278d121b", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a field.\nUnramified quasi-compact morphisms <MATH_0002> are affine.\nThis is true because <MATH_0003> has dimension <MATH_0004> and is Noetherian,\nhence is a finite discrete set, and each point gives an affine open,\nso <MATH_0005> is a finite disjoint union of affines hence affine.\nNoether normalization forces <MATH_0006> to be the spectrum of a finite\n<MATH_0007>-algebra <MATH_0008>.\nThis algebra is a product of finite separable field extensions of <MATH_0009>.\nThus, an unramified quasi-compact morphism to <MATH_0010>\ncorresponds to a finite number of finite separable field extensions of <MATH_0011>.\nIn particular, an unramified morphism with a connected source and a one point\ntarget is forced to be a finite separable field extension.\nAs we will see later, <MATH_0012> is <ACCENT_0001>tale if and\nonly if it is unramified. Thus, in this case at least, we obtain a very easy\ndescription of the <ACCENT_0002>tale topology of a scheme. Of course, the cohomology of\nthis topology is another story.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:288cfc2283bd4ed4c6896ac5a17e2923e9cef1a1f1053ef59ed3137d3628e81c", "unit_id": "inventory:etale:024X:example/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale:inventory:etale:024Z:example/0001", "hash": "sha256:286c3c71298a379b16546ed39f50dd20c2fe528e6d9a6277c089238b4e8147f8", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 32702, "byte_start": 31234, "file": "etale.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:f2674c83f7845962d1b987ec70d0b11c8ad606bf1943c6953c16c0c89468f14f", "line_end": 831, "line_start": 805}, "owner_tag": "024Z", "parent_tag": "024W", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "024W", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "LOCKED_0001": "\\label{example-number-theory-etale}", "MATH_0001": "$L/K$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_L$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_K$", "MATH_0004": "$K \\to L$", "MATH_0005": "$f : \\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_L) \\to \\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_K)$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_L)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_L$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Omega_{\\mathcal{O}_L/\\mathcal{O}_K}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{O}_K$", "MATH_0012": "$K$", "MATH_0013": "$L$", "MATH_0014": "$X$", "MATH_0015": "$\\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_L)$", "MATH_0016": "$X \\to \\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_K)$", "MATH_0017": "$L/K$", "MATH_0018": "$Y$", "MATH_0019": "$\\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_K)$", "MATH_0020": "$X \\to Y$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{example}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{example}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6a23364921de7776750741f4c7cccebbebbc06fb0d575cc7e2034aa6ca9db9b2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0f1f8122cd66c60c7b3685524bc3a2bacd46e97075ad0e38a359c9610c30add8", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nFix an extension of number fields <MATH_0001> with rings of integers\n<MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003>. The injection <MATH_0004> defines a\nmorphism <MATH_0005>.\nAs discussed above, the points where <MATH_0006> is unramified in our sense\ncorrespond to the set of points where <MATH_0007> is unramified in the conventional\nsense. In the conventional sense, the locus of ramification in\n<MATH_0008> can be defined by vanishing set of the\ndifferent; this is an ideal in <MATH_0009>. In fact, the different is\nnothing but the annihilator of the module\n<MATH_0010>. Similarly, the\ndiscriminant is an ideal in <MATH_0011>, namely it is the\nnorm of the different.\nThe vanishing set of the discriminant is precisely the set\nof points of <MATH_0012> which ramify in <MATH_0013>.\nThus, denoting by <MATH_0014> the complement of the closed subset\ndefined by the different in <MATH_0015>,\nwe obtain a morphism <MATH_0016> which is unramified.\nFurthermore, this morphism is also flat, as any local homomorphism\nof discrete valuation rings is flat, and hence this morphism is\nactually <ACCENT_0001>tale. If <MATH_0017> is finite Galois, then denoting by\n<MATH_0018> the complement of the closed subset defined by the discriminant in\n<MATH_0019>, we see that we get even a\nfinite <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism <MATH_0020>.\nThus, this is an example of a finite <ACCENT_0003>tale covering.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4a69747b0398364da1d926e71fdfef7bdc0ff6cc9aa3bc6438ddc8dff1921918", "unit_id": "inventory:etale:024Z:example/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-reference:algebra:inventory:algebra:00T6:definition/0001:algebra-definition-standard-smooth", "hash": "sha256:58fcc9c07a325ab1b29b1e0f650d58799670cd678be82fa2fc9c7d00ade6895d", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 1365440, "byte_start": 1364347, "file": "algebra.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:35c749a69cee0d61ddca47110fbc4f9d6d7011ba129cca43517503a1358bfa38", "line_end": 37271, "line_start": 37235}, "owner_tag": "00T6", "parent_tag": "00T1", "requested_label": "algebra-definition-standard-smooth", "requested_tag": "00T6", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "algebra", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00T1", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{definition-standard-smooth}", "MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$n \\geq c \\geq 0$", "MATH_0003": "$f_1, \\ldots, f_c \\in R[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nR[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]/(f_1, \\ldots, f_c)\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "MATH_0006": "$$\ng =\n\\det\n\\left(\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\partial f_1/\\partial x_1 &\n\\partial f_2/\\partial x_1 &\n\\ldots &\n\\partial f_c/\\partial x_1 \\\\\n\\partial f_1/\\partial x_2 &\n\\partial f_2/\\partial x_2 &\n\\ldots &\n\\partial f_c/\\partial x_2 \\\\\n\\ldots & \\ldots & \\ldots & \\ldots \\\\\n\\partial f_1/\\partial x_c &\n\\partial f_2/\\partial x_c &\n\\ldots &\n\\partial f_c/\\partial x_c\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right)\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$R[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]/(f_1, \\ldots, f_c)$", "MATH_0008": "$R$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$R \\to S$", "MATH_0011": "$n \\geq c \\geq 0$", "MATH_0012": "$f_1, \\ldots, f_c \\in R[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]$", "MATH_0013": "$R[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]/(f_1, \\ldots, f_c)$", "MATH_0014": "$R$", "MATH_0015": "$S$", "MATH_0016": "$R[x_1, \